------------------------------- MODULE Model -------------------------------
(***************************************************************************)
(* The cdn.pokoin.com serving path (docs/SERVING_PIPELINE.md, phase 1):    *)
(* the remote-managed Cloudflare tunnel `pokoin-cdn` with one ingress rule *)
(* `http://pokoin-cdn-origin:18081` and two connectors, one on the Pi      *)
(* (`cloudflared-cdn.service`, the name bound in /etc/hosts) and one in    *)
(* nezopt k3s (Deployment `cloudflared-cdn`, the name bound by a Service). *)
(*                                                                         *)
(* Per host: the live name binding, the boot template cloud-init rewrites  *)
(* it from, the origin (Rust CDN) up or down, the connector connected or   *)
(* not. Cloudflare sends a request to any connected connector and never    *)
(* looks behind it: a connector whose origin is down or unresolvable stays *)
(* connected and answers 502. Around it: the sentinel's probe and alert,   *)
(* and the SPA's image-fallback memo (one browser, a page of card images). *)
(*                                                                         *)
(* Time is a bounded clock: one Tick is one sentinel period (5 min).       *)
(*                                                                         *)
(* Fixed = TRUE is the pipeline design (every feature flag on).            *)
(* Fixed = FALSE with every flag off is the system of 28/29 Oct 2026.      *)
(***************************************************************************)
EXTENDS Naturals, FiniteSets, TLC

CONSTANTS
    Pi, K3s,              \* the two connector hosts
    None,                 \* no connector
    Urls,                 \* card images on one page (siblings of a card collapsed)
    Missing,              \* images whose file really is missing on the CDN
    Fixed,                \* the pipeline design: every flag below on
    PersistBinding,       \* Apply renders the binding into the live file AND the boot template
    OriginGatedConnector, \* connector starts only on a healthy origin and a watchdog stops it
    PublicProbe,          \* the sentinel fetches a real object through the public URL
    PathProbe,            \* the sentinel checks every connector path on its own (resolve, fetch, connected)
    BurstAwareMemo,       \* the memo never marks dead from a burst; dead marks live DeadTTL
    WatchdogTicks,        \* periods a gated connector may stay connected to a bad origin
    AlertAfter,           \* consecutive failing probes before the alert (sentinel `confirm`)
    DeadTTL,              \* periods a dead mark may outlive a healthy CDN (D5)
    DeadKeep,             \* today's dead-mark lifetime (24 h; any value > DeadTTL)
    CanReboot,            \* hosts the environment may reboot
    CanCrash,             \* hosts whose origin may crash (outside a reboot)
    CanDrift,             \* hosts whose binding something outside the pipeline may remove
    MaxDrifts             \* drifts per host (finitely many: D3's premise)

Hosts == {Pi, K3s}
\* Hosts whose binding is /etc/hosts regenerated by cloud-init. K3s binds the
\* name through the Service `pokoin-cdn-origin`; its manifest is its template.
HostsFile == {Pi}

ASSUME Fixed => PersistBinding /\ OriginGatedConnector /\ PublicProbe /\ PathProbe /\ BurstAwareMemo
ASSUME Missing \subseteq Urls /\ Urls \ Missing # {}
ASSUME CanReboot \subseteq Hosts /\ CanCrash \subseteq Hosts /\ CanDrift \subseteq Hosts /\ MaxDrifts \in Nat
ASSUME WatchdogTicks >= 1 /\ AlertAfter >= 1 /\ DeadTTL >= 1 /\ DeadKeep > DeadTTL

\* Lifetime of a dead mark.
MarkTTL == IF BurstAwareMemo THEN DeadTTL ELSE DeadKeep
MaxAge == IF DeadKeep > DeadTTL THEN DeadKeep ELSE DeadTTL

Codes == {"none", "200", "502", "530"}   \* 530: Cloudflare with no connector (error 1033)

VARIABLES
    live,        \* live[h]: pokoin-cdn-origin resolves on h now
    tmpl,        \* tmpl[h]: the boot template (cloud-init / k8s manifest) has the binding
    up,          \* up[h]: the origin CDN process on h answers
    conn,        \* conn[h]: h's cloudflared-cdn is connected to Cloudflare
    applied,     \* applied[h]: the pipeline's Apply has run on h
    badFor,      \* badFor[h]: whole periods h has been connected to a bad origin
    probeDue,    \* this period's sentinel run has not happened yet
    streak,      \* consecutive failing sentinel runs (capped at AlertAfter)
    alerted,     \* the sentinel alert is raised
    outage,      \* whole consecutive periods in which some public request could 5xx
    goodSeen,    \* this period has had a state where every public request answers 200
    dead,        \* dead[u]: the memo holds `about:dead` for u
    age,         \* age[u]: periods since u was marked dead
    healthyDead, \* healthyDead[u]: periods u has stayed dead while the CDN served every request
    last,        \* ghost: the last public request, <<connector, status>>
    everAlerted, \* ghost: an alert has been raised
    burstMarked, \* ghost: a page load with no healthy connector created a dead mark
    rebootedApplied, \* ghost: the Pi rebooted after Apply
    drifted,     \* ghost: drifted[h]: the binding was removed outside the pipeline since the last Apply
    drifts,      \* drifts[h]: how many times h has drifted (bounded by MaxDrifts)
    degraded,    \* degraded[h]: whole consecutive periods in which h does not serve
    servedSeen,  \* servedSeen[h]: h has served at some point of this period
    repair       \* ghost: Pi drift repair stage, 0 none, 1 drifted, 2 alerted, 3 re-applied, 4 served

vars == <<live, tmpl, up, conn, applied, badFor, probeDue, streak, alerted, outage, goodSeen,
          dead, age, healthyDead, last, everAlerted, burstMarked, rebootedApplied,
          drifted, drifts, degraded, servedSeen, repair>>

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
(* Derived state. The Of-forms take the variables as arguments so Track   *)
(* can evaluate them on the next state.                                    *)

HealthyOf(h, u, l) == u[h] /\ l[h]
\* Some request could get a 5xx: no connector, or a connected one with a bad origin.
PublicBadOf(c, u, l) == (\A h \in Hosts : ~c[h]) \/ (\E h \in Hosts : c[h] /\ ~HealthyOf(h, u, l))

\* h's connector path serves: connected, origin up and resolvable.
ServesOf(h, c, u, l) == c[h] /\ HealthyOf(h, u, l)

Healthy(h) == HealthyOf(h, up, live)
Serves(h) == ServesOf(h, conn, up, live)
Connected == {h \in Hosts : conn[h]}
PublicBad == PublicBadOf(conn, up, live)
\* Some request can be served 200.
CanServe == \E h \in Connected : Healthy(h)
\* Every request is served 200.
AllServe == ~PublicBad

TypeOK ==
    /\ live \in [Hosts -> BOOLEAN] /\ tmpl \in [Hosts -> BOOLEAN]
    /\ up \in [Hosts -> BOOLEAN] /\ conn \in [Hosts -> BOOLEAN]
    /\ applied \in [Hosts -> BOOLEAN]
    /\ badFor \in [Hosts -> 0..WatchdogTicks + 1]
    /\ probeDue \in BOOLEAN /\ streak \in 0..AlertAfter /\ alerted \in BOOLEAN
    /\ outage \in 0..AlertAfter + 1 /\ goodSeen \in BOOLEAN
    /\ dead \in [Urls -> BOOLEAN] /\ age \in [Urls -> 0..MaxAge]
    /\ healthyDead \in [Urls -> 0..DeadTTL + 1]
    /\ last \in (Hosts \cup {None}) \X Codes
    /\ everAlerted \in BOOLEAN /\ burstMarked \in BOOLEAN /\ rebootedApplied \in BOOLEAN
    /\ drifted \in [Hosts -> BOOLEAN] /\ drifts \in [Hosts -> 0..MaxDrifts]
    /\ degraded \in [Hosts -> 0..AlertAfter + 1] /\ servedSeen \in [Hosts -> BOOLEAN]
    /\ repair \in 0..4

\* 27 Oct: the Pi's binding was a hand edit of /etc/hosts, not in the template.
\* K3s: the Service is in the applied manifest. Everything up and connected.
Init ==
    /\ live = [h \in Hosts |-> TRUE]
    /\ tmpl = [h \in Hosts |-> h \notin HostsFile]
    /\ up = [h \in Hosts |-> TRUE]
    /\ conn = [h \in Hosts |-> TRUE]
    /\ applied = [h \in Hosts |-> FALSE]
    /\ badFor = [h \in Hosts |-> 0]
    /\ probeDue = TRUE /\ streak = 0 /\ alerted = FALSE
    /\ outage = 0 /\ goodSeen = TRUE
    /\ dead = [u \in Urls |-> FALSE] /\ age = [u \in Urls |-> 0]
    /\ healthyDead = [u \in Urls |-> 0]
    /\ last = <<None, "none">>
    /\ everAlerted = FALSE /\ burstMarked = FALSE /\ rebootedApplied = FALSE
    /\ drifted = [h \in Hosts |-> FALSE] /\ drifts = [h \in Hosts |-> 0]
    /\ degraded = [h \in Hosts |-> 0] /\ servedSeen = [h \in Hosts |-> TRUE]
    /\ repair = 0

\* Variables the actions below set themselves; Track derives the rest.
core == <<live, tmpl, up, conn, applied, probeDue, streak, alerted, dead, age, last,
          everAlerted, burstMarked, rebootedApplied, drifted, drifts, repair>>
\* The variables only Drift, Apply, Probe and Request touch.
driftVars == <<drifted, drifts, repair>>

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
(* Hosts                                                                   *)

\* Power cycle. cloud-init (`manage_etc_hosts: True`) regenerates /etc/hosts
\* from the template; the origin and the connector come up again later.
Reboot(h) ==
    /\ h \in CanReboot
    /\ live' = [live EXCEPT ![h] = tmpl[h]]
    /\ up' = [up EXCEPT ![h] = FALSE]
    /\ conn' = [conn EXCEPT ![h] = FALSE]
    /\ rebootedApplied' = (rebootedApplied \/ (h = Pi /\ applied[Pi]))
    /\ UNCHANGED driftVars /\ UNCHANGED <<tmpl, applied, probeDue, streak, alerted, dead, age, last, everAlerted, burstMarked>>

\* Someone adds the line to /etc/hosts by hand (28 Oct). Live file only.
ManualEdit(h) ==
    /\ h \in HostsFile /\ ~live[h]
    /\ live' = [live EXCEPT ![h] = TRUE]
    /\ UNCHANGED driftVars /\ UNCHANGED <<tmpl, up, conn, applied, probeDue, streak, alerted, dead, age, last,
                   everAlerted, burstMarked, rebootedApplied>>

\* Something outside the pipeline removes the binding from the live file
\* AND the template: an OS / cloud-init upgrade overwrites the template, the
\* Service is deleted, the host is reinstalled. Not fair.
Drift(h) ==
    /\ h \in CanDrift /\ drifts[h] < MaxDrifts
    /\ live' = [live EXCEPT ![h] = FALSE]
    /\ tmpl' = [tmpl EXCEPT ![h] = FALSE]
    /\ drifted' = [drifted EXCEPT ![h] = TRUE]
    /\ drifts' = [drifts EXCEPT ![h] = @ + 1]
    /\ repair' = IF h = Pi THEN 1 ELSE repair
    /\ UNCHANGED <<up, conn, applied, probeDue, streak, alerted, dead, age, last, everAlerted,
                   burstMarked, rebootedApplied>>

\* The pipeline's `pokoin-infra apply h`: writes the rendered binding.
\* Fixed: the live file and the boot template. Today there is no pipeline:
\* the "apply" is the same live-only hand edit. A k8s Service is always
\* persistent. It runs once on first deploy, and again whenever the binding
\* is incomplete while an alert is raised: weak fairness on Apply is "an
\* alert is acted on" (the operator runs `pokoin-infra apply`). Without the
\* alert there is nothing to act on, and nothing repairs a broken binding.
Apply(h) ==
    /\ ~applied[h] \/ (alerted /\ (~live[h] \/ ~tmpl[h]))
    /\ applied' = [applied EXCEPT ![h] = TRUE]
    /\ live' = [live EXCEPT ![h] = TRUE]
    /\ tmpl' = [tmpl EXCEPT ![h] = IF PersistBinding \/ h \notin HostsFile THEN TRUE ELSE @]
    /\ drifted' = [drifted EXCEPT ![h] = FALSE]
    /\ repair' = IF h = Pi /\ repair = 2 THEN 3 ELSE repair
    /\ UNCHANGED <<up, conn, probeDue, streak, alerted, dead, age, last, everAlerted,
                   burstMarked, rebootedApplied, drifts>>

OriginCrash(h) ==
    /\ h \in CanCrash /\ up[h]
    /\ up' = [up EXCEPT ![h] = FALSE]
    /\ UNCHANGED driftVars /\ UNCHANGED <<live, tmpl, conn, applied, probeDue, streak, alerted, dead, age, last,
                   everAlerted, burstMarked, rebootedApplied>>

OriginRecover(h) ==
    /\ ~up[h]
    /\ up' = [up EXCEPT ![h] = TRUE]
    /\ UNCHANGED driftVars /\ UNCHANGED <<live, tmpl, conn, applied, probeDue, streak, alerted, dead, age, last,
                   everAlerted, burstMarked, rebootedApplied>>

\* systemd / the Deployment starts cloudflared. Fixed: only behind an
\* ExecCondition that resolves the origin name and fetches through it.
ConnStart(h) ==
    /\ ~conn[h]
    /\ OriginGatedConnector => Healthy(h)
    /\ conn' = [conn EXCEPT ![h] = TRUE]
    /\ UNCHANGED driftVars /\ UNCHANGED <<live, tmpl, up, applied, probeDue, streak, alerted, dead, age, last,
                   everAlerted, burstMarked, rebootedApplied>>

\* Fixed: the watchdog stops a connector whose origin no longer answers.
\* Today nothing stops it (cloudflared's /ready only reports the tunnel).
ConnStop(h) ==
    /\ OriginGatedConnector
    /\ conn[h] /\ ~Healthy(h)
    /\ conn' = [conn EXCEPT ![h] = FALSE]
    /\ UNCHANGED driftVars /\ UNCHANGED <<live, tmpl, up, applied, probeDue, streak, alerted, dead, age, last,
                   everAlerted, burstMarked, rebootedApplied>>

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
(* Cloudflare, the sentinel, the browser                                   *)

\* A public request: Cloudflare picks any connected connector.
Request ==
    /\ IF Connected = {}
         THEN last' = <<None, "530">> /\ UNCHANGED repair
         ELSE \E h \in Connected :
                /\ last' = <<h, IF Healthy(h) THEN "200" ELSE "502">>
                /\ repair' = IF repair = 3 /\ h = Pi /\ Healthy(h) THEN 4 ELSE repair
    /\ UNCHANGED <<live, tmpl, up, conn, applied, probeDue, streak, alerted, dead, age,
                   everAlerted, burstMarked, rebootedApplied, drifted, drifts>>

\* One `pokoin-ops sentinel` run per period. Today it sees a dead origin
\* process (failed unit, closed port, metrics unreachable) and nothing else.
\* Fixed: `pokoin-infra verify` inside the sentinel. PublicProbe: a real
\* object through the public URL fails whenever a request could 5xx.
\* PathProbe: per host, resolve the name, fetch a real object through that
\* host's origin, and check its connector is connected; fails when any one
\* path does not serve, even while the other leg serves everything.
\* One streak, one alert (see README).
Probe ==
    /\ probeDue
    /\ LET fail == \/ \E h \in Hosts : ~up[h]
                   \/ PublicProbe /\ PublicBad
                   \/ PathProbe /\ \E h \in Hosts : ~Serves(h)
           s == IF fail THEN (IF streak < AlertAfter THEN streak + 1 ELSE AlertAfter) ELSE 0
       IN /\ streak' = s
          /\ alerted' = (s >= AlertAfter)
          /\ everAlerted' = (everAlerted \/ s >= AlertAfter)
          /\ repair' = IF repair = 1 /\ s >= AlertAfter THEN 2 ELSE repair
    /\ probeDue' = FALSE
    /\ UNCHANGED <<live, tmpl, up, conn, applied, dead, age, last, burstMarked, rebootedApplied,
                   drifted, drifts>>

\* The browser renders a page: every image not marked dead is requested,
\* each one through any connected connector (ImageOk / ImageFail per URL).
\* Today every failure becomes `about:dead` for 24 h. Fixed: a page whose
\* every image failed is an outage, not missing files, and marks nothing.
PageLoad ==
    LET L == {u \in Urls : ~dead[u]}
        CanOk(u) == u \notin Missing /\ CanServe
        CanFail(u) == u \in Missing \/ PublicBad
    IN
    /\ L # {}
    /\ \E fails \in SUBSET L :
         /\ \A u \in L \ fails : CanOk(u)
         /\ \A u \in fails : CanFail(u)
         /\ LET marks == IF BurstAwareMemo /\ fails = L THEN {} ELSE fails IN
              /\ dead' = [u \in Urls |-> dead[u] \/ u \in marks]
              /\ age' = [u \in Urls |-> IF u \in marks THEN 0 ELSE age[u]]
              /\ burstMarked' = (burstMarked \/ (~CanServe /\ marks # {}))
    /\ UNCHANGED driftVars /\ UNCHANGED <<live, tmpl, up, conn, applied, probeDue, streak, alerted, last,
                   everAlerted, rebootedApplied>>

\* The dead mark's keepMs has passed (checked on the next load()).
MemoExpire(u) ==
    /\ dead[u] /\ age[u] >= MarkTTL
    /\ dead' = [dead EXCEPT ![u] = FALSE]
    /\ age' = [age EXCEPT ![u] = 0]
    /\ UNCHANGED driftVars /\ UNCHANGED <<live, tmpl, up, conn, applied, probeDue, streak, alerted, last,
                   everAlerted, burstMarked, rebootedApplied>>

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
(* Time                                                                    *)

\* Every step but Tick: the counters follow the next state.
Track ==
    /\ badFor' = [h \in Hosts |-> IF conn'[h] /\ ~HealthyOf(h, up', live') THEN badFor[h] ELSE 0]
    /\ outage' = IF PublicBadOf(conn', up', live') THEN outage ELSE 0
    /\ goodSeen' = (goodSeen \/ ~PublicBadOf(conn', up', live'))
    /\ healthyDead' = [u \in Urls |-> IF dead'[u] THEN healthyDead[u] ELSE 0]
    /\ degraded' = [h \in Hosts |-> IF ServesOf(h, conn', up', live') THEN 0 ELSE degraded[h]]
    /\ servedSeen' = [h \in Hosts |-> servedSeen[h] \/ ServesOf(h, conn', up', live')]

T(A) == A /\ Track

Cap(n, m) == IF n < m THEN n ELSE m

\* One sentinel period passes. It cannot pass a deadline: this period's
\* sentinel run, the watchdog's bound, a dead mark's expiry.
Tick ==
    /\ ~probeDue
    /\ OriginGatedConnector =>
         \A h \in Hosts : ~(conn[h] /\ ~Healthy(h) /\ badFor[h] >= WatchdogTicks)
    /\ \A u \in Urls : ~(dead[u] /\ age[u] >= MarkTTL)
    /\ probeDue' = TRUE
    /\ badFor' = [h \in Hosts |-> IF conn[h] /\ ~Healthy(h) THEN Cap(badFor[h] + 1, WatchdogTicks + 1) ELSE 0]
    /\ outage' = IF goodSeen THEN 0 ELSE Cap(outage + 1, AlertAfter + 1)
    /\ goodSeen' = AllServe
    /\ age' = [u \in Urls |-> IF dead[u] THEN Cap(age[u] + 1, MaxAge) ELSE 0]
    /\ healthyDead' = [u \in Urls |-> IF dead[u] /\ AllServe THEN Cap(healthyDead[u] + 1, DeadTTL + 1) ELSE 0]
    /\ degraded' = [h \in Hosts |-> IF servedSeen[h] THEN 0 ELSE Cap(degraded[h] + 1, AlertAfter + 1)]
    /\ servedSeen' = [h \in Hosts |-> Serves(h)]
    /\ UNCHANGED <<live, tmpl, up, conn, applied, streak, alerted, dead, last, everAlerted,
                   burstMarked, rebootedApplied, drifted, drifts, repair>>

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Next ==
    \/ \E h \in Hosts :
         \/ T(Reboot(h)) \/ T(ManualEdit(h)) \/ T(Drift(h)) \/ T(Apply(h))
         \/ T(OriginCrash(h)) \/ T(OriginRecover(h))
         \/ T(ConnStart(h)) \/ T(ConnStop(h))
    \/ T(Request) \/ T(Probe) \/ T(PageLoad)
    \/ \E u \in Urls : T(MemoExpire(u))
    \/ Tick

\* Fair: time, the sentinel, the pipeline, connector start and the watchdog,
\* memo expiry. Not fair: reboots, crashes, recoveries, hand edits, drift,
\* requests, page loads.
Spec ==
    /\ Init /\ [][Next]_vars
    /\ WF_vars(Tick) /\ WF_vars(T(Probe))
    /\ \A h \in Hosts : WF_vars(T(Apply(h))) /\ WF_vars(T(ConnStart(h))) /\ WF_vars(T(ConnStop(h)))
    /\ \A u \in Urls : WF_vars(T(MemoExpire(u)))

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
(* Properties (docs/SERVING_PIPELINE.md D1-D5)                             *)

\* D1: once Apply has run on h, the origin name resolves on h in every later
\* state, through any interleaving of reboots and hand edits. Only an
\* explicit Drift can remove it, and detecting that is D4b's job.
RebootSafety == \A h \in Hosts : (applied[h] /\ ~drifted[h]) => live[h]

\* D2: a connector Cloudflare can route to has a healthy, resolvable origin,
\* except for at most WatchdogTicks whole periods after the origin went bad
\* (the watchdog's detection delay; a request in that window gets a 502).
NoFalseFailover == \A h \in Hosts : (conn[h] /\ ~Healthy(h)) => badFor[h] <= WatchdogTicks

\* D3 (liveness): an origin that eventually stays up is eventually and for
\* ever serving through its connector, so requests are served 200. Premise
\* beyond <>[]up[h]: finitely many drifts (MaxDrifts). After the last one,
\* PathProbe's alert and Apply's fairness restore the binding.
Availability == \A h \in Hosts : (<>[]up[h]) => <>[](conn[h] /\ Healthy(h))

\* D4: more than AlertAfter whole periods in which public requests could get
\* a 5xx imply the alert is raised.
Detection == outage > AlertAfter => alerted

\* D4b: more than AlertAfter whole periods in which one host does not serve
\* imply the alert, even while the other host serves every request. A reboot
\* shorter than that is expected and silent.
RedundancyDetection == \A h \in Hosts : degraded[h] > AlertAfter => alerted

\* D5: an image that exists is never kept dead more than DeadTTL periods of
\* a fully serving CDN, and a page load with no healthy connector (an
\* outage-wide burst) never creates a dead mark.
ClientRecovery ==
    /\ \A u \in Urls \ Missing : healthyDead[u] <= DeadTTL
    /\ ~burstMarked

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
(* Witnesses: must be VIOLATED by the fixed model (the behaviour happens). *)

\* The Pi reboots after Apply and serves a 200 again.
NeverServedAfterReboot == ~(rebootedApplied /\ last = <<Pi, "200">>)
\* The Pi origin is down and K3s serves the request.
NeverFailover == ~(~up[Pi] /\ last = <<K3s, "200">>)
\* An alert is raised and later resolved.
NeverAlertRecovered == ~(everAlerted /\ ~alerted)
\* A really missing image is still remembered as dead (the memo still works).
NeverDeadMark == \A u \in Missing : ~dead[u]
\* The Pi drifts, the alert fires, Apply runs, and the Pi serves a 200 again.
NeverDriftRepaired == repair # 4

=============================================================================
